# arm32 vectors of the alu16 group (Thumb-2 code): the state after each case of
# cases/alu16.cases under qemu-arm-static (-cpu max) over 3 states a case, written by
# write_arm32_vectors in crates/ra-asm-lift/tests/vectors/arm32.rs and replayed by its arm32 test.
# case <kind> <bytes> <assembly> <- <template>; in: the registers the case sets (the rest are
# zero), the flags as NZCV bits, the window of data bytes; out: where the case stopped and
# what it changed.
case Alu 081c adds r0, r1, #0 <- adds {Ld}, {Ln}, #{imm3}
in nzcv=0100 r0=0xb r1=0x80000009
out pc=0x30002002 sig=trap r0=0x80000009 nzcv=1000
case Alu 081c adds r0, r1, #0 <- adds {Ld}, {Ln}, #{imm3}
